Without any huge spoilers (because I don't know them all):

If you want to zap it at a monster, zap it at a monster with
some unusual magic ability.  Think of a wand of cancellation
more as a wand of /magic/ cancellation.  Rothes, and most other
monsters, are quite mundane and would be unaffected.  Note, a
cancelled mind flayer will still happily eat your brain, so try
not to learn that one the hard way. 

The second great usefulness of the /WoC is when you zap it at an
item or stack of items.  Experiement with this cautiously at
first, with fully identified items that you comfortably assume
are in some way magical. Blessings/curses, enchantments, many
potions, wands, books and scrolls will all be affected by the
wand. 

The complete spoiler is to be found somewhere online, I'm sure
I've read about this in Dylan's quides, but hope these hints get
you on the right track. 

